			<div class="content" id="post-content-4825011">
									

<p><strong>DISCLAIMER: I am a newbie and I <em>cannot</em> give green-lights.</strong></p>
<p><strong><span style="text-decoration: underline;">Please take everything I say with a grain of salt</span></strong></p>
<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">This is a placeholder, I will give my thoughts on this as soon as I can</span></p>
<p>So besides some <em><span style="text-decoration: underline;">grammer and formatting issues</span></em> which I'm sure some others shall go over, I'll go ahead and tell you what I really enjoy about the SCP and what I'm really confused about it.</p>
<hr />
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">What I like about this concept</span></p>
<p>1. It's an interesting concept. An old man who ensures his captivity area is perfectly smooth via the use of shadows is definitely a new concept. One that can adapt to his environment and understand the humans around him is definitely an interesting trait. I also enjoy the use of shadows.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">READ&nbsp;MORE</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">READ&nbsp;LESS</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p><span style="text-decoration: underline;">What I'm confused about or dislike about this concept</span></p>
<p>So there's quite a bit I'm confused about. I definitely believe you need to flesh out the story and SCP idea in-general. I recommend spending more time on your SCP concept and think &quot;how does this pertain to the story I'm trying to tell?&quot;, &quot;how does this tell us about the Foundation?&quot;, and &quot;what seems to be missing?&quot;.</p>
<p><em>The biggest advice I can give you is that the concept overall needs to be refined</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p>except he is always facing the corner of a room facing magnetic north at midnight and every two hours moves to another corner.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>1. How does he face the corner of a room he's in if he faces the magnetic north? In my opinion, I don't believe the changing of corners or facing magnetic north needs to be added here as it doesn't pertain to your central narrative you are trying to tell.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>His face is always in shadow nothing can be done to see it or probe it</p>
</blockquote>
<p>2. How is his face always in shadow? Does he somehow have something covering his face? I'm not necessarily sure what you meant by this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>He must always be kept in a perfectly square room made of concrete with an aggregate of bone and seashell one of the few objects he cannot destroy.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>3. <em>Why</em> is this? I understand he can't destroy those materials, but it is never explained that the SCP destroys the room.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The SCP does this by creating a black shadow around itself that engulfs the room no light can enter this shadow and any who enter are turned to bone and blood.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>3. This might be a bit petty but I don't think that's a shadow. A shadow is emitted via the use of light and an object blocking the light from reaching a surface. This seems more like a aura or &quot;circular radius&quot;.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The walls must be perfectly smooth any cracks or chips in the wall causes the SCP to react and turn the room back to a perfect square.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>4. Do the walls normally become cracked? The SCP seems to already make sure that his room is as smooth as butter when it comes to cracks and chips. There seems to be no reason for this to be one of the things the Foundation has to look out for. I believe this is a simple misunderstanding of what you're trying to say.</p>
<p>I believe you're trying to say &quot;if the room the SCP is contained in has any imperfection around it, such as an object or crack in the wall, it will cause the SCP to react&#8230;&quot;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The initial discovery of the SCP in Canada comes first along with a new mobile task force called the Canada goose.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>4. Why the need for a new mobile task force? In my opinion, I don't believe there is a need for one. Also I recommend giving more detail into your SCP's discovery.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The next is an incident involving a chip in the wall and the SCP’s reaction then two files hidden by 05 council. Then a new test which gives a hint to removed files and finally placing the SCP in a perfectly round room.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>5. Although I like the idea you're going for, why hide the files? If the files are supposed to be hidden for no one besides the O5-council (meaning that it is <span style="text-decoration: underline;">EXTREMELY HIDDEN</span>) then it shouldn't be referenced afterwards in the following file? I recommend not adding this in. It could work, but needs some rethinking.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The next is an incident involving a chip in the wall</p>
</blockquote>
<p>6. Where are these chips coming from? Are they coming from the SCP? If the chip on the wall makes the SCP enact dangerous actions, explain that the Foundation is trying to ensure these &quot;chips in the wall&quot; don't occur.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>There is more to the SCP than what we see it is hinted he knows foundation secrets.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>7. This isn't well explained enough. How do we know the SCP knows more than what he sees? Does he explain it in some way?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>An old man</p>
</blockquote>
<p>8. So it's a humanoid SCP. Does he talk in some way? How does him being &quot;an old man&quot; relate to how he acts or how the story is? Remember he technically acts like a human since he's an old man. Read here for more about writing humanoid SCPs in the &quot;Humanoids&quot; tab: <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/how-to-write-an-scp">http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/how-to-write-an-scp</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p>The initial discovery</p>
</blockquote>
<p>9. Ok so, how does the SCP react when it's outside and not in a corner? If it's never been out of a corner because it's impossible, how did the Foundation manage to contain the SCP? Where was he located in the first place? Try to give more detail in this.</p>
<hr /></div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, its definitely an idea I think you could make work, but it definitely needs a lot of rework and re-evaluation to ensure the concept given is solid before asking for critique. Remember, don't let these comments discourage you, and try to take the criticism you get as a way to improve your concept.</p>
<p>Good luck to you, feel free to PM on wikidot and I'll gladly come back to see your idea once you feel that you reworked it enough. :)</p>

							</div>

								
