<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Here, have a Placeholder. I'll crit this within 24 hours.</span></p>
<p>I was summoned by IRC Chat. Let's crit this.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[+]&nbsp;Here,&nbsp;have&nbsp;some&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">[-]&nbsp;OK,&nbsp;now&nbsp;give&nbsp;me&nbsp;back&nbsp;my&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>he is always facing the corner of a room facing magnetic north at midnight</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How is he always facing the corner of a room <em>and</em> the magnetic north? What happens if the room's corners don't align with the magnetic north?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>His face is always in shadow nothing can be done to see it or probe it.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>How is his face always hidden? SCP-096 is also secretive about its face and the Foundation has managed to get pictures of it. You need to explain <em>how</em> is this possible.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>bone and seashell one of the few objects he cannot destroy.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Then&#8230; he can destroy everything else? Why is precisely bone and seashell the things that he cannot destroy? I'm feeling like you're trying to give the man too many powers and abilities. Maybe it would be better to keep the anomaly within the creepiness of a guy always facing a corner.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The walls must be perfectly smooth any cracks or chips in the wall causes the SCP to react and turn the room back to a perfect square.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Why is he triggered by this? I get that he wants to always face a corner, but why a simple crack would bother him? Also, how did they contain him? How did they get him inside a containment cell? I think it would be better to make this a localional anomaly. Maybe they can't remove him from a specific room? Maybe he <em>and</em> the room are anomalous?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The SCP does this by creating a black shadow around itself that engulfs the room no light can enter this shadow and any who enter are turned to bone and blood.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is why I think you are adding too many powers to the anomaly. This seems unnecessary, as it appears to not serve anything in the story.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Central Narrative:</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What is all of this? What are those documents about? What is the objective of the man? Why is the O5 Council afraid of him? You may want to keep these things a mystery within the article, but reviewers need to know what you're trying to do. Also, keeping too many things secret may bore the reader.</p>
<p>In my opinion, this concept seems to have various clichés from the Series I skips.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I personally would suggest you to stick around for a little longer before trying to write an article.</p>
<p>Feel free to contact a member of the <a href="http://scp-wiki.wikidot.com/butterfly-squad-roster">Butterfly Squad</a> to get more crit, or PM me to take another look.</p>

